sequenceDiagram
  participant Caller as Coordinator / Engine.run
  participant Eng as Engine
  participant Sch as DependencyScheduler
  participant Fn as @step function
  participant Ctx as StepContext
  participant Emt as EventEmitter
  participant WD as Work dir
  participant Spool as Spool FS

  Caller->>Eng: _run_attempt(plan, context with execution_id)
  note right of Caller: execution_id allocated first,<br/>ordered after every recorded attempt
  Eng->>Emt: emit(plan.attempt_started, step inventory)
  Emt->>Spool: {execution_id}_plan_attempt_started.json
  Eng->>Eng: preflight (ids, deps, cycles, policy, outputs, callables)
  opt plan rejected
    Eng->>Emt: emit(plan.attempt_report, preflight_rejected)
    Eng--xCaller: raise PreflightValidationError (no step ran)
  end
  Eng->>WD: write plan.json
  loop while the scheduler has a ready step (all deps succeeded or reused)
    Sch-->>Eng: next ready step (plan-list order breaks ties)
    Eng->>WD: ensure {plan_id}/{step_id}/
    Eng->>Eng: fingerprint = fp(params + input digests + declared outputs)
    alt marker matches and every declared output exists
      Eng->>Emt: emit(step.skipped, reason=cache_hit)
      Emt->>Spool: {step_id}/{run_id}/0001_step_skipped.json
      Eng->>Sch: reused (satisfies dependents)
    else run required
      Eng->>WD: remove success.fingerprint
      Eng->>Ctx: create (run_id, fingerprint, required outputs, correlation)
      Eng->>Fn: call(ctx, **params)
      Ctx->>Emt: emit(step.started)
      Emt->>Spool: {step_id}/{run_id}/0001_step_started.json
      alt step returns and its declared outputs exist
        Ctx->>Emt: emit(step.succeeded)
        Emt->>Spool: 000N_step_succeeded.json
        Eng->>WD: replace success.fingerprint atomically
        Eng->>Sch: succeeded (dependents may become ready)
      else step raises, or a declared output is missing
        Ctx->>Emt: emit(step.failed)
        Emt->>Spool: 000N_step_failed.json
        opt transient error
          Eng->>Emt: emit(step.retry_unimplemented)
        end
        alt fail_fast
          Eng->>Emt: emit(plan.attempt_report, failed_fast)
          Eng--xCaller: raise (later steps unreached, no marker written)
        else continue_independent
          Eng->>Sch: failed
          Sch-->>Eng: newly blocked dependents
          Eng->>Emt: emit(step.blocked) for each
          Emt->>Spool: {step_id}/{execution_id}_step_blocked.json
        end
      end
    end
  end
  note over Eng,Spool: event-publication or marker failure, or cancellation<br/>between steps, ends the attempt under either policy;<br/>its report is then published unless event publication is what failed
  Eng->>Emt: emit(plan.attempt_report, completed, with every outcome and blocker)
  Emt->>Spool: {execution_id}_plan_attempt_report.json
  Eng-->>Caller: drained report (outcome failed if any step failed or was blocked)
  note right of Caller: coordinator records a finished request's<br/>outcome and token on the plan document
